 of Santiago. <br>3. Senior Royal Chaplain (traditionally held by the Archbishop of Santiago) <br>3. Grand Almoner <br>3. Grand Inquisitor (either a bishop or archbishop)<br>4. Bishop: In the Americas: “The king personally nominated bishops and abbots to the pope. Members of a cathedral chapter were selected by either the king or the Council of Indies from a list of three names submitted by the bishop. The crown normally delegated the appointment of parish priests to the viceroy or governor.” <br>5. Royal Confessor: "Those religious who had previously served as royal preachers or confessors, as provincials and generals of their orders, as university professors and as theological advisors (calificadores) to the inquisition all became major contenders for promotion to the Castilian episcopal bench." <br>5. Royal Preachers: "Those religious who had previously served as royal preachers or confessors, as provincials and generals of their orders, as university professors and as theological advisors (calificadores) to the inquisition all became major contenders for promotion to the Castilian episcopal bench." <br>6. Lesser Royal Chaplains <br>7. Abbot . In the Americas: “The king personally nominated bishops and abbots to the pope. Members of a cathedral chapter were selected by either the king or the Council of Indies from a list of three names submitted by the bishop. The crown normally delegated the appointment of parish priests to the viceroy or governor.” <br>8. Parish Priest: In the Americas: “The king personally nominated bishops and abbots to the pope. Members of a cathedral chapter were selected by either the king or the Council of Indies from a list of three names submitted by the bishop. The crown normally delegated the appointment of parish priests to the viceroy or governor.” <br>9. Deacon<br>9. Prior<br>10. Friar<br>10. Monk<br>10. Nun<br>10. Overseas Missionaries <br><ul><li>“Until 1559 the crown had little direct influence on the church in the Netherlands.” </li><li>“The church in the Italian kingdoms continued to operate in the canonical way, which is to say that cathedral chapters nominated bishops to the pope.” </li></ul>\n                    '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1638, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 1529})
